<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish June consumer prices rise 0.3 pct m/m - CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish June consumer prices rise 0.3 pct m/m - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish June consumer prices, as measured by the consumer price index, rose 0.3 percent on the month, the Central Statistics Office (CSO) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a rise of 0.2 percent on May while a year-on-year comparison was not available due to a lack of data for June last year.  </p>
<p>On a 13-month basis, the index rose 1.8 percent from May 1996.</p>
</text>
